Subject: Gives the register number paths their tag-specific fast cases: int32 bitwise/shift and inline double compare-branches

What this does
  Gives the register number paths their tag-specific fast cases: int32 bitwise/shift and inline double compare-branches.

Why we need it
  Every `&`/`\.

What it adds
  `/`^`/`<<`/`>>`/`>>>` on two int32 operands and every `<`/`<=`/`>`/`>=` on two doubles called the engine slow path, which re-tests tags the register VM had already tested.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
